          "content": "```python\ndef longest_common_subsequence(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the length of the longest common subsequence of strings a and b.\n\n    Uses dynamic programming with O(min(len(a), len(b))) extra memory.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Use the shorter string for the DP row to minimize memory usage.\n    if len(a) < len(b):\n        short, long = a, b\n    else:\n        short, long = b, a\n\n    dp = [0] * (len(short) + 1)\n\n    for ch_long in long:\n        # prev holds the diagonal value from the previous row: dp[j - 1].\n        prev = 0\n        for j, ch_short in enumerate(short, start=1):\n            temp = dp[j]\n            if ch_long == ch_short:\n                dp[j] = prev + 1\n            else:\n                dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[j - 1])\n            prev = temp\n\n    return dp[-1]\n```",
